      }
    ],
    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Do you have a sweet tooth? It might "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " your DNA."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Researchers from the University of Colorado found that almost 500 different "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "genes",
            "zh": "基因"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " directly influence what we choose to eat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“Our "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " is influenced by several factors. The most common ones include "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "socio-economic status",
            "zh": "社会经济地位"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and culture,” said Joanne Cole. She is a professor of "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "genomics",
            "zh": "基因组学"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " at the University of Colorado. “"
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", there also is a real genetic influence on the foods we choose to eat.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Several of the genes Cole studied were related to "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "sensory pathways",
            "zh": "感官通路"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". One well-known "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " is the bitter taste "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "receptor",
            "zh": "苦味受体"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " TAS2R38. It controls the ability to taste bitterness. This gene interacts with a chemical found in "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Brussels sprouts",
            "zh": "抱子甘蓝"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and cabbage. This chemical gives these foods their bitter taste. "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", some people are born to hate Brussels sprouts and cabbage."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "A "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " explanation might be behind why some people have a sweet tooth. “Some people might have a strong genetic preference for sweeter foods,” Cole said. “This is controlled by the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "binding",
            "zh": "结合"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of sugars to certain receptors in their sensory system. Then the pleasure region in their brain is "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ".”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Our DNA can also influence our preference for healthier foods. “In my earlier research, I discovered two genes influencing fruit "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "intake",
            "ref": "v-intake"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ",” Cole said. “People with these genes also reported "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " intake of added sugar.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Scientists want to improve our understanding of the genes that drive our dietary preferences. This may help to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " our brains to choose healthier food."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p8",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“"
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "Flavour",
            "ref": "v-flavour"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " is the number one "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of food choice,” Cole said. “So I would like to use this information to make healthier food more flavourful. We can also make diet plans based on genes.” This will make it easier for people to keep a healthy diet."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
